  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maryland received $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.2% year over year. The state recorded 3,575 awards with an average award size of $297K. FY22 obligations totaled $43B, FY23 obligations totaled $42.6B, FY24 obligations totaled $47.4B, FY25 obligations totaled $40.7B, and FY26 obligations totaled $38.5B. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $355M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $218M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $156M in FY2027 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $211M, Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $192M, and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $159M in FY2027 to date. GUIDEHOUSE INC. received $159M, THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC received $132M, and C&T TECHNOLOGIES LLC received $38.6M in FY2027 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 buying in Maryland compare with recent years?",
        "body": "FY27 obligations in Maryland are $1.1B through the fiscal year to date. Obligations in each of the five prior fiscal years were larger: FY22 $43B, FY23 $42.6B, FY24 $47.4B, FY25 $40.7B, and FY26 $38.5B. Obligations fell 97.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which buyers and industries dominate Maryland federal spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer with $355M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $218M and the Department of the Interior with $156M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences leads industries with $211M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $192M and Other Computer Related Services with $159M."
      }
    ]
  },
